{"id": 1919559, "name": "DeLORME v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO.", "name_abbreviation": "DeLorme v. Atlantic Coast Line R. R.", "decision_date": "1908-02-25", "docket_number": "6765", "first_page": "370", "last_page": "372", "citations": [{"type": "official", "cite": "79 S.C. 370"}], "court": {"name_abbreviation": "S.C.", "id": 8894, "name": "Supreme Court of South Carolina"}, "jurisdiction": {"id": 59, "name_long": "South Carolina", "name": "S.C."}, "cites_to": [{"cite": "76 S, C., 30", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "opinion_index": -1}, {"cite": "63 S. C., 169", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [2350676], "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/sc/63/0169-01"]}, {"cite": "78 S. C., 36", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [1917238], "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/sc/78/0036-01"]}, {"cite": "78 S. C., 36", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [1917238], "opinion_index": 0, "case_paths": ["/sc/78/0036-01"]}], "analysis": {"cardinality": 224, "char_count": 2751, "ocr_confidence": 0.46, "pagerank": {"raw": 4.277134884225609e-08, "percentile": 0.2701402668649794}, "sha256": "4d06ce5538717583c586d6d95236ab6895e0210bc09977be8b68674aa83785b8", "simhash": "1:8e099e9a4e2d8fd2", "word_count": 450}, "last_updated": "2024-02-27T20:09:51.886260+00:00", "provenance": {"date_added": "2019-08-29", "source": "Harvard", "batch": "2018"}, "casebody": {"judges": [], "parties": ["DeLORME v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO."], "opinions": [{"text": "-The opinion of the Court was delivered 'by\nMr. Justice Jones.\nThis is an. appeal by defendant from a judgment of the Circuit 'Court affirming the judgment of a magistrate for loss of freight while in the possession of the defendant, $7.13, .and the statutory penalty, $50.00, for failure to adjust the loss within ninety days.\nAppellant, under its first exception, endeavors toi raise the question -as to the constitutionality of -the act approved May 13, A. D. 1903, entitled \u201c An act to' further define -connecting lines of comm|on carriers and to fix their liabilities.\u201d There is, however, no basis, for the exception in the record. No liability of a connecting carrier is involved; the undisputed- evidence being that the goods were delivered to defendant and the 'loss' accrued while in defendant\u2019s possession.\nUnder the second' exception, appellant as-sail's thie -constitutionality of the penalty statute approved February 33, 1903, entitled \u201cAn act to regulate the manner in which common-carriers doing business in this State shall adjust freight -charges- -and claims- for the loss- of or damla-ge to freight.\u201d This question is settled against appellant 'by the case of Charles v. Atlantic Coast Line R. R. Co., 78 S. C., 36, which has been approved in. other cases.\nThe remaining exceptions, alleging the total absence of evidence to sustain 'the judgment, can not be sustained. The original bill of lading introduced in evidence showed receipt by defendant of six boxes of crackers 'Consigned to plaintiff, Greellyville, S. C., and defendant\u2019s receipt to' the plaintiff -consignee at Greelyville, S. C'., for freight charges on five of said boxes and acknowledging shortage of one box (for loss- of wbi-cb the suit was brought) showed that the loss occurred while the goods- were in defendant\u2019s possession.\nThe judgment of the Court -is affirmed.", "type": "majority", "author": "Mr. Justice Jones."}], "attorneys": ["Messrs. J. T. Barron and Purdy & O\u2019Brien, for appellant.", "Messrs. Dams & Weinberg, contra,"], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "6765\nDeLORME v. ATLANTIC COAST LINE R. R. CO.\n1. Railroads. \u2014 The Act, 24 Stat., 1, relating to liability of connecting carriers does not apply to a shipment over one line.\n2. Ibid. \u2014 Constitutional Law. \u2014 The Act, 24 Stat., 81 relating to adjustment of loss of or damage to freight is held constitutional in Charles v. B. B., 78 S. C., 36, and that case is followed here.\nBefore Memminger, J., Clarendon,\nJune, 1907.\nAffirmed.\nAction 'by M. DeLorme against Atlantic Coast L-ine Railroad Cbmpany. From judgment for plaintiff, defendant appeals.\nThis case was not printed in numerical order because copy was mislaid.\nMessrs. J. T. Barron and Purdy & O\u2019Brien, for appellant.\nNo .argument.\nMessrs. Dams & Weinberg, contra,\ncite: Penalty act is constitutional: 63 S. C., 169; 73 St \u20ac., 71, 140; 78 & C., 3'6. Freight receipt shows it was received by defendant: 76 S, C., 30-8.\nFebruary 25, 1908."}, "file_name": "0370-01", "first_page_order": 382, "last_page_order": 384}